<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  KarpaChess's own privacy manifest.

  The app collects nothing: no account, no analytics, no network access. Every
  lesson, puzzle, game and preference stays on the device, so both collected
  data types and tracking domains are empty, and NSPrivacyTracking is false.
  That matches "Data Not Collected" in App Store Connect.

  The app's OWN Dart and Swift code uses no required-reason API: it never
  reads a file timestamp, free disk space, the system boot time or the active
  keyboard list. Its file work is File.exists() and a rename
  (core/io/atomic_write.dart, core/io/stored_files.dart), neither on Apple's
  list.

  Most plugins that do reach such an API declare it themselves, and Apple
  aggregates those with this file: shared_preferences_foundation (UserDefaults,
  CA92.1), path_provider_foundation and image_picker_ios (file timestamps).
  The Stockfish module declares its own — its Syzygy loader references fstat —
  in packages/karpa_engine/ios/Resources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy.

  file_picker is the exception, and the reason FileTimestamp is declared below.
  (This is the macOS copy of ios/Runner/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy; keep the two in
  step, since the same plugins are linked into both apps.)
  file_picker_darwin 1.0.1 lists `.process("Resources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy")`
  in its Package.swift but does not ship that file, so the build prints
  "Invalid Resource 'Resources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy': File not found" and the
  plugin's declaration never reaches the binary. Its code does use the APIs:
  `contentsOfDirectory(atPath:)` and `resourceValues(forKeys: [.fileSizeKey])`
  over the app's tmp directory (C617.1 — metadata of files inside the app
  container), and `attributesOfItem(atPath:)` over files the reader chose in a
  document picker (DDA9.1 — files the user specifically granted access to).
  Declaring them here is accurate for this binary, which links that code, and
  an under-declaration is what gets an upload rejected (ITMS-91053). Drop this
  entry only once file_picker actually ships its own manifest.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
				<string>DDA9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
